==Battleground==
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Hackey]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The objective of this stage is to kill some Rain Ds, all without losing too much terrain, as you do not want Hackey to reach your base. The general idea is to either rush down Rain D with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or to simply meatshield and slowly kill each Rain D with a powerful attacker, such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. Just stall the Rain Ds with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] until you have enough money to spawn your Uber, then time it so Hackey doesn't kill it.

Or you could use [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and Research [[Cat Combo]]s to solo any crown difficulty. Courier has to be high enough leveled (preferably lv.50), so he can two-hit knockback the Rain D.s. Do note that this strategy is fairly inconsistent.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] unit can aid greatly in dealing with the Rain D.s. [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]], [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Gothic Mitama]], and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]] specifically are very well suited for this job.

